1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:02,060
Two criminals died beside Jesus that afternoon.

2
00:00:02,901 --> 00:00:03,441
Same nails.

3
00:00:04,041 --> 00:00:04,541
Same hill.

4
00:00:05,201 --> 00:00:05,761
Same distance.

5
00:00:06,801 --> 00:00:07,721
Opposite eternities.

6
00:00:07,841 --> 00:00:08,442
Both guilty.

7
00:00:09,002 --> 00:00:09,962
Both just as close.

8
00:00:10,722 --> 00:00:11,442
Both spoke.

9
00:00:12,042 --> 00:00:14,883
If thou be Christ, save thyself and us.

10
00:00:15,323 --> 00:00:16,863
A taunt, not a prayer.

11
00:00:16,963 --> 00:00:18,243
The other thief rebuked him.

12
00:00:18,823 --> 00:00:22,104
And we indeed justly; for we receive the due

13
00:00:22,164 --> 00:00:25,425
reward of our deeds: but this man hath done

14
00:00:25,565 --> 00:00:26,485
nothing amiss.

15
00:00:26,765 --> 00:00:27,365
A confession.

16
00:00:28,145 --> 00:00:29,585
A verdict: innocent.

17
00:00:30,606 --> 00:00:31,406
Then one request.

18
00:00:32,006 --> 00:00:35,406
Lord, remember me when thou comest into thy

19
00:00:35,446 --> 00:00:35,826
kingdom.

20
00:00:36,367 --> 00:00:40,647
Verily I say unto thee, To day shalt thou be

21
00:00:40,687 --> 00:00:42,608
with me in paradise.

22
00:00:42,808 --> 00:00:43,728
He asked for someday.

23
00:00:44,648 --> 00:00:46,208
Jesus gave him that same afternoon.

24
00:00:46,348 --> 00:00:46,848
No merit.

25
00:00:47,289 --> 00:00:48,649
Just repentance and trust.

26
00:00:48,769 --> 00:00:50,309
We are all one of those two men.

27
00:00:50,509 --> 00:00:51,569
Ask what the thief asked.

28
00:00:52,289 --> 00:00:52,809
Remember me.

29
00:00:53,950 --> 00:00:54,730
Then hear his answer.

30
00:00:55,870 --> 00:00:56,230
With me.

31
00:00:57,090 --> 00:00:57,430
Today.

32
00:00:58,531 --> 00:00:58,971
Paradise.
